Subject: Re: Fill Matrix with Vector of Row Numbers: Summary
Message-ID: <20050901144344.D29AC3BC193@poros.telenet-ops.be>

Apparently their are a number of ways to solve my question.
Here are the inputs I've received. In a way they all seem to be alike, but
there are differences. I've used the first option because it's the shortest
one. 

First option:

ind <- c(4,6,8,9,12)
w <- matrix(0, 20, length(ind))
w[seq(0, length(w) - 1, nrow(w)) + ind] <- 1 w

Second option:

rownumbers<- c(4, 6, 8, 9, 12)
period <- paste("W", 1:160, sep = "")
final.matrix <- matrix(0, nrow = length(period), ncol = length(rownumbers))
dimnames(final.matrix)[[2]] <- paste("Col", 1:length(rownumbers))
dimnames(final.matrix)[[1]] <- period
for(i in 1:length(rownumbers)){
final.matrix[rownumbers[i],i] <- 1
}

Third Option:

vv <- c(4,6,8,9,12)
pp <- 1:160
mm <- matrix(0, length(pp), length(vv))
dimnames(mm) <- list(paste("W", pp, sep=""),
                     paste("C", vv, sep=""))
mm[vv,] <- diag(length(vv))
mm[c(1:15,158:160),]

Thx a lot
Bert

